 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Set the three server-only variables listed in `.env.example` in the server's runtime
+environment (or your deployment platform's secret configuration). Sign-up uses Twilio Verify to deliver and validate
+SMS codes before forwarding account credentials to the existing registration API.
+Without these variables, sign-up reports that SMS verification is unavailable;
+it never accepts a placeholder code. Configure the Verify service for **6-digit**
+codes and the default **10-minute** expiry.
+
+For automatic code extraction, configure an origin-bound SMS template in Twilio
+whose final line is `@your-public-hostname #123456` (substitute Twilio's code
+variable for `123456`). The hostname must match the HTTPS page hosting sign-up,
+without a scheme or path. See [Chrome's WebOTP SMS format](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp)
+and [Twilio Verify templates](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api/templates).
+The form requests WebOTP with user consent where supported and also provides
+`autocomplete="one-time-code"`, numeric keyboard input, paste, and manual entry.
+No automatic submission occurs when a code is extracted.
+
+The local endpoint binds verification to the server session and normalized phone,
+limits checks to five per challenge, and enforces a 30-second resend cooldown.
+Configure provider Fraud Guard, geographic permissions, and deployment-level rate
+limits for public traffic; session cooldowns alone do not prevent SMS abuse.
+The external registration API remains independently accessible and must enforce
+verification itself if verification is required for *all* account creation.
+This integration verifies phone ownership for this app's sign-up flow; it does
+not persist phone numbers in the external account API, whose current contract
+only accepts username and password.
+
+Run the mocked sign-up API checks with `node --experimental-strip-types --test tests/signup.test.ts` (Node 24+). No SMS is sent by these tests.
